{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"cfe77f003e65e3c77e855a8ea37afcab888b6eead4c9d253cf7714d666947aa1","digest":{"component_or_area":"scripts/gen_env_registry.py - environment variable registry generator","key_entities":["scripts/gen_env_registry.py","scripts/gen_env_registry.py:98","docs/env-vars.md","os.environ.get","os.environ.pop","os.environ.setdefault","os.environ.__getitem__","os.getenv","KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS","opcert_service/config.py","_io/import_ndjson.py","scripts/check_config_ownership.py","tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py","REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY","REBAR_SYNC_PUSH"],"problem_keywords":["environment variable documentation","registry generator","silent omission","os.environ accessor recognition","documentation drift"],"propositions":["The generator recognizes only os.environ.get, os.environ[...], and os.getenv forms, causing alternative read patterns like os.environ.pop to silently disappear from the generated registry without error or warning.","Changing os.environ.get to os.environ.pop for the same key results in undocumented environment variables that ship with passing CI, violating the stated invariant that new env-var reads cannot ship undocumented.","The scanner must classify all os.environ attribute accesses (get, pop, setdefault, __getitem__) as key-bearing or bulk, and raise an exception on unrecognized forms rather than silently skipping them.","make lint does not run the generator's --check gate, so contributors discover documentation staleness only in the full CI suite, creating a feedback loop weaker than the drift gate's guarantees."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","eve